   <h3> Fire Giant Raid! BH Invited!</h3>
   <p>
   
<ul>
<li><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=415&lastnode_id=925">Front Page</a>
</ul>




<table border=0 width=100% cellspacing=0>
<tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white>Fire Giant Raid! BH Invited!</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=335&lastnode_id=925">Gyrak</a> on 2000-12-05 14:19:58</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>OOC<br>
<br>
We have been invited by the leader of Prelude to Entropy, to join them in a Fire Giant raid in SOL B this coming Saturday, Dec 9th. Most likely around 12, noon Central time. Theyt are a new guild with an impressive number of lvl 46 and higher folks for a guild so new. I am friends with most of these people and can vouch for them in saying they are an excellent group of people to hunt with and I have full confidence in their abilties. They also have several clerics and enchanters amongst them which can be a big plus. The only draw back is that they are not an "evil race" guild. They do not even RP. They just play to have fun. So the decision to go is yours or not. I plan on going and I hope others around the lvls 42 or higher (if healer class) and probably at least 45 or higher if melee class, join us there as well. This can be a good chance for BH to work on working together as well with other guilds when it comes to raids, in which case we will be doing alot of, for along time still. For any who comes, please take Runja's advice on such things and come prepared. Even tho it will not be a true RP environment, we will still be represnting the Blood Horde and should be prepared. (have you a map if you do not know the zone and do alittle research on the zone and Fire Giants as well) This guild has shown interest in teaming with us for future raids such as Hate and Fear and so on, and with the people we have now, and with the ones we will have over 46 in the next few weeks, along with their people, it is very possible we could start doing raids together. Our two guilds would actually compliment each other very well. Any questions, you can contact me, or RAGABASH, whom is their WarLord. Hope to see you all there!<br>
<br>
GYRAK SOULSTEALER</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>

<tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=926&lastnode_id=925">Re: Fire Giant Raid! BH Invited!</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=215&lastnode_id=925">Razze</a> on 2000-12-06 01:41:33</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2> Please count me in I will be there, and I have my map. Plus I need that torque that the giant king has. see you there<br>
Razze</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=927&lastnode_id=925">Re: Fire Giant Raid! BH Invited!</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=673&lastnode_id=925">Duraden</a> on 2000-12-07 19:54:27</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>Yes I also know several Prelude to Entropy guildmembers and they are indeed great people to group with. I will do my best to make it to this event also.  I think its important to start making contacts and friends for later on when the hordes strength has amassed to the point where we can raid the Planes of the gods. </td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=929&lastnode_id=925">Re: Fire Giant Raid! BH Invited!</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=335&lastnode_id=925">Gyrak</a> on 2000-12-08 12:33:29</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>The time has been set for this to begin at 1:00 Central Time, Saturday. The 9th of December. Again I stress if you do not know this part of the zone, such as myself, be as prepared as possible and have you a map of this zone. Preluse to Entropy will set the loot rules and such, but as Duraden said, we should view this more as a learning experience amongst our selves and with other guilds. Although we are growing quickly, and strongly. It will be sometime before we could raid the lairs of the Gods on our own. Such contacts with guilds like these, can prove to be extremly helpful. Hope to see you all there!<br>
<br>
Gyrak Soulstealer</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>
